<title>GHANA: Ghana February yr-on-yr inflation at 30.6 percent.</title>
<headline>Ghana February yr-on-yr inflation at 30.6 percent.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana's government statistical service issued the following updated price inflation figures:</p>
<p>Y/y change (pct):</p>
<p>					 Feb 1997: 30.6</p>
<p>					 Jan 1997: 31.5</p>
<p>					 Feb 1996: 68.0</p>
<p>Index (1977 =  100):</p>
<p>					Feb 1997: 79,841.0</p>
<p>					Jan 1997: 77,477.1</p>
<p>					Feb 1996: 61,154.4</p>
<p>Prices in the month of February showed an increase of 3.0 percent, a setback on 2.5 percent in January 1996.</p>
<p>The government's objective is to reduce year-on-year inflation to 15 percent by December 31, 1997.</p>
</text>
